In C, there is no built-in way to terminate a program. However, you can use the `exit` function to end the program and return a status code to the operating system. Here's how you can do it:

```c
#include <stdlib.h>

int main() {
    exit(0);  // Replace 0 with the status code you want to return
    return 0;
}
```

In this example, the program will terminate immediately and return a status code of 0 to the operating system. The `exit` function is declared in the `<stdlib.h>` header file, so make sure to include that when using this function.
